        "original_id": "8c2e1fb1-8c7d-5c52-8c2e-fd07032f6010",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Fort Davis, Alaska; Army Peak; Alaska\n- People: Jefferson C. Davis\n- Organizations: United States Army\n- Roles: military commander of Alaska; regular officer\n- Events: American Civil War\n\nFacts:\n- Jefferson C. Davis was born on March 2, 1828.\n- Jefferson C. Davis served as the military commander of Alaska from 1868 to 1870.\n- Jefferson C. Davis was a regular officer of the United States Army during the American Civil War.\n- Jefferson C. Davis was known for the similarity of his name to Confederate President Jefferson Davis and for killing a superior officer in 1862.\n- Jefferson C. Davis died on November 30, 1879.\n- Fort Davis in Alaska was established in 1900.\n- Fort Davis in Alaska was named for General Jefferson C. Davis.\n- Army Peak likely derived its name from the United States Army's presence in the area after Fort Davis was established in 1900.",
